arker more  villainous version of themselves  specifically jessica henwick and reggae  jean-page it's like taking a holiday  from the british just kind of you flush  all of the politeness out of your system  he describes it as leaning into all the  things that you would normally never do  and seeing how far that can take you i  surprised myself when i was told to yell  at chris and they said just go go as far  as you can jessica is unsure if that's  the take that was used in the final cut  but apparently she was foaming at the  mouth as the primary example of exactly  what not to do in acid retrieval  number four the hot trunk ryan gosling  was stuck in for two days this was fun  trying to figure out how this would go  down you know getting hit with a dart  like that we are definitely enjoying the  use of his word fun it led to two more  days being in a hot trunk and frog which  was not as much fun luckily though  anadare moss saving the day yet again  was taking great care of him while in  the driver's seat  apparently she's a great driver and he  felt very safe back there aside from the  sweltering heat what gives you the  impression that they care what i think  this is my career you understand number  five the incredible julia butters is  already making history she's worked with  so many legends in the industry from the  russo brothers to steven spielberg and i  said i've been wanting to work with  julia butter since i was a teenager  my favorite answer to anything ever  we're with you billy bob the improvised  moment comes into play when they are  actually on a close-up of chris julia  had already shot her close-up scene i  was about to turn and leave and i turned  back and i said kick his ass normally  she would never go off script like that  they said all right we're gonna do your  close-up again because we really liked  that and i was so excited number six and  all the reshoots that came with it oh i  wish it would have been a question the  cast spent months 